---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "March 1, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service - prod.bd" description="Terms of Service for the prod.bd tunnel service.">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-24 pb-20">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_p]:text-gray-700 [&_p]:leading-relaxed [&_p]:mb-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:mb-4 [&_ul]:text-gray-700 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_a]:text-green-600 [&_a]:underline">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">Effective date: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the prod.bd service ("Service"), operated by Prod.bd ("we", "us", "our"). By accessing or using the Service, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, you must not use the Service.</p>

      <h2>1. Service Description</h2>
      <p>prod.bd provides secure HTTP tunnel infrastructure that enables users to expose locally running development servers to the public internet through assigned subdomains. The Service is offered under free and paid subscription tiers.</p>

      <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>You must be at least 16 years of age to use the Service. By using the Service, you represent and warrant that you meet this requirement and have the legal capacity to enter into these Terms.</p>

      <h2>3. Account Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>You are solely responsible for safeguarding your client identifiers, API tokens, and any credentials associated with your account. You accept responsibility for all activities that occur under your account. You must notify us promptly of any unauthorized use.</p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use the Service to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Transmit content that is unlawful, defamatory, fraudulent, or otherwise objectionable</li>
        <li>Distribute malware, conduct phishing, or facilitate any form of cyberattack</li>
        <li>Violate any applicable local, national, or international law or regulation</li>
        <li>Interfere with, degrade, or disrupt the integrity or performance of the Service</li>
        <li>Attempt to circumvent usage limits, rate controls, or access restrictions</li>
        <li>Resell, sublicense, or redistribute access to the Service without prior written consent</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate any account or tunnel that violates these Terms, without prior notice and at our sole discretion.</p>

      <h2>5. Subscription Plans and Billing</h2>
      <p>The Service is available under the following plans:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Free</strong> — 10,000 requests per month, 1 GB bandwidth per month</li>
        <li><strong>Pro ($5/month)</strong> — 100,000 requests per month, 5 GB bandwidth per month</li>
        <li><strong>Team ($20/month)</strong> — 1,000,000 requests per month, 10 GB bandwidth per month</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Paid subscriptions are billed on a monthly recurring basis. Usage exceeding the included allowances on Pro and Team plans is subject to overage charges of $1.00 per 10,000 additional requests and $0.25 per additional GB of bandwidth. Overage is calculated at the end of each billing cycle.</p>
      <p>All fees are stated in United States Dollars (USD) and are exclusive of applicable taxes. You are responsible for any taxes associated with your use of the Service.</p>

      <h2>6. Refund Policy</h2>
      <p>If you are not satisfied with the Service, you may request a full refund within fourteen (14) calendar days of your initial paid subscription purchase. Refund requests must be submitted to <a href="mailto:support@prod.bd">support@prod.bd</a>.</p>
      <p>Following the fourteen-day refund window, you may cancel your subscription at any time. Cancellation will take effect at the conclusion of the current billing period. No prorated or partial refunds will be issued for the remaining unused portion of a billing cycle.</p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>The Service, including its software, design, and documentation, is the intellectual property of Prod.bd and is protected by applicable copyright and intellectual property laws. The prod.bd CLI and worker are released under the MIT License. These Terms do not grant you any rights to our trademarks, service marks, or trade names.</p>

      <h2>8. Service Availability and Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>We endeavor to maintain high availability of the Service; however, we do not guarantee uninterrupted, error-free, or secure operation. The Service is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis, without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including but not limited to implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.</p>

      <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Prod.bd and its officers, directors, employees, and agents shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including but not limited to loss of profits, data, or business opportunities, arising out of or in connection with your use of or inability to use the Service, regardless of the theory of liability.</p>
      <p>Our total aggregate liability for any claims arising under these Terms shall not exceed the amount you have paid to us in the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to the claim.</p>

      <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
